D-GLOSSARY-BUILD-LOSES-TO-A-RAIL-THE-PLA.verified_at_the_data_2026_08_24:
🔴 I HAD INFERRED THE PIN FROM A DOCSTRING. Verified against the store, and it is stronger than 'a rail happened to be pinned':

    loreweave_agent_registry.mode_bindings, system row:
        mode = 'write'  ->  workflows {vision-to-book}
        mode = 'plan'   ->  skills    {plan_forge}

So the WRITE MODE PINS vision-to-book ON EVERY TURN, for every user of this deployment — it is not conditional on the request's words. The harness sends permission_mode='write' by default (fe_runner: sc.get('permission_mode', 'write')) and the glossary-build scenario does not override it, which is the ordinary case rather than a fixture quirk: a user asking to build their world is on a write turn.

AND THE SEED IS WHAT PUTS THE RAIL ON THE COMPETING STEPS. vision-to-book's first three steps are the standards setup; the scenario seeds an adopted ontology to satisfy this tool's OWN precondition, which advances the rail to 3/9 — so its next actionable steps are exactly 4/5/6 (ontology_read -> extract_entities_from_doc -> propose_entities). Removing the seed does not help: measured earlier, with no ontology the model does standards setup and never reaches the tool either. The rail wins from both starting states.

